  "dom_id": "step-q160794",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\u27e8\\frac{1}{3-t},\\,\\sqrt{t+2},\\,{e}^{2t}\u27e9.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\frac{1}{3-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\sqrt{t+2}$ is $t\\in [-2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{2t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076578/assets/39a4299fea0f2137e79490cce9e4660f0c1b021f0de9977090cc3a572df41b1f.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in [-2,3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$",
